  <p>How the dates were counted: business days only, skipping the US federal holidays on Nov. 26, Dec. 25 and Jan. 1. Two business days between approved files and the in-market date, for platform review and scheduling. Three between delivered files and approval, for one consolidated round of sign-off. Seven of production, the top of the studio's published window for a full launch batch. Two for the written proposal. The review and sign-off allowances are this page's planning assumptions, not measurements, because no platform, carrier or survey publishes a creative lead time. Swap in your own team's numbers and the rows move with them.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">Thanksgiving falls on Thursday, Nov. 26, 2026, Christmas on Friday, Dec. 25, and New Year's Day on Friday, Jan. 1, 2027.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: US Office of Personnel Management, federal holidays 2026 and 2027, read Oct. 8, 2026. Government holiday list.</p>

  <p>Black Friday and Cyber Monday follow from that: the day after Thanksgiving and the Monday after it. Europe runs Black Friday on the same Friday without the Thursday holiday, so a European team gains a working day in late November.</p>

  <h2>Which platform deadlines actually bind?</h2>

  <p>Only a handful of dates in the season are set by someone other than you. They are the ones worth building the plan around, because no amount of overtime moves them.</p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Platform or carrier</th>
          <th scope="col">What it publishes</th>
          <th scope="col">What it means for the plan</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Meta (Facebook, Instagram)</th>
          <td>Most ads reviewed within 24 hours; any creative edit starts a new review</td>
          <td>Submit two business days before the ad has to run</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">TikTok</th>
          <td>Most ads reviewed within 24 hours; a creative edit triggers a review of up to 24 hours</td>
          <td>Same two days</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Google Ads</th>
          <td>Most ads reviewed within one business day; submit several days ahead for a fixed date</td>
          <td>Same two days, more for new landing pages</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Google Merchant Center</th>
          <td>Submit promotions at least 24 hours before they start</td>
          <td>One business day, Monday to Friday</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Amazon (US store)</th>
          <td>Black Friday Week and Cyber Monday deals submitted by Oct. 20; A+ review up to seven business days</td>
          <td>Deals locked 38 days before Black Friday</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">USPS</th>
